dt-bindings: power: rockchip: allow resets on a power domain

Some domains come up with the bus behind them in an undefined state, and an
access before their resets are pulsed can hang it. The nodes are closed with
unevaluatedProperties: false, so describing the resets in a device tree needs
them in the schema first.

Signed-off-by: Isaiah DeRose-Wilson <isaiahdw@gmail.com>

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/rockchip,power-controller.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/rockchip,power-controller.yaml
@@ -136,6 +136,14 @@
 
       domain-supply:
         description: domain regulator supply.
+
+      resets:
+        minItems: 1
+        maxItems: 8
+        description: |
+          A number of resets that need to be pulsed after the domain powers
+          on. Some domains come up with the bus behind them in an undefined
+          state, and an access before the pulse can hang it.
 
       pm_qos:
         $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle-array
